{
 "_note": "Part rigs of the six Krypta bosses (Story 1) that drew as atlas sprites: knochenwaechter, grabmutter, nekromantenfuerst, truhenfresser, archivar, leerenbrut. Same format as rigs.json (rects are inclusive [x0,y0,x1,y1] on the source frame, each opaque pixel belongs to the first part whose rect contains it, hp values are weights scaled to the boss HP, a destroyed vital part kills; items have their own image with grip/hand/rest/tip; \"disables\" lists the actions a part or item carries: the crypt action name plus the Story attack ids of tools/krypta_dungeon/krypta_monsters.js STATS). Loaded by src/rig/rig_library.gd after companion_rigs.json. Source frames are pixel_art painted by the crypt's own painter (krypta_monsters.js render: idle frame 0, the Truhenfresser's teeth frame) at ART pixel size, i.e. the atlas frame itself (def w x h, feet on the bottom row), so a def's \"rig\" copies the rig at def.scale (src/hell/drake_rig_host.gd adopt_looks) and the vfx_glow anchors keep their meaning. The held weapon was painted without and is its own item (k=2, outline included) so it can be knocked away; frame-animated extras (sparkles, glow dots, the Fuerst's soul flame) were left out (the flame is \"burn\"). \"points\" (mouth, core) are where the bosses' attacks start (drake_rig_host.gd muzzle: bolt, breath, homing, lob and sweep from mouth, the rest from core).",
